    "The consultation is 15 minutes -- a direct conversation about what you are dealing with, how long it has been present, and whether IFS and EMDR are the right fit for your specific situation. No forms, no obligation. For Alameda veterans and first responders who are skeptical about therapy, the consultation is where that skepticism gets an honest answer rather than a sales pitch. If working together makes sense, the first full session assesses the scope of the work, maps the internal parts most active in creating the difficulty, and begins direct work with them. Sessions are 45 or 60 minutes via secure telehealth video, Wednesday through Friday.",
    "IFS sessions work with specific internal parts directly -- honoring what each part was built for while helping the internal system update to current circumstances. For Alameda clients whose parts developed in high-stress environments, this means working with the hypervigilant part, the shut-down part, the part that does not ask for help, and understanding what each is still protecting. The work is respectful of the history that shaped those parts and focused on helping them operate differently in the present.",
    "EMDR sessions process specific experiences or patterns of experience the nervous system has not fully integrated. For Alameda veterans and first responders, the processing often involves working through accumulated occupational exposure rather than a single incident -- which means the work unfolds across multiple sessions as layers of experience are addressed systematically. The bilateral stimulation activates natural processing capacity in a way that allows stored responses to update without requiring extensive verbal narration of difficult material.",
