    "IFS sessions are structured and purposeful -- not open-ended conversations that drift but direct engagement with specific parts of the internal system. Each session has a clear focus. The driven part, the anxious part, the self-critical part, the exhausted part underneath all of it. Getting curious about what each is protecting rather than trying to manage or suppress it produces the kind of internal shift that changes how patterns operate rather than just how well they are managed. For Emeryville clients who appreciate structured, outcome-oriented work, IFS fits that preference while producing change at a deeper level than behavioral approaches.",
    "EMDR sessions target specific experiences or memory networks systematically. Each session processes a defined target rather than exploring broadly, which means progress is trackable and the scope of the work is clear. For Emeryville professionals whose anxiety or stuck patterns have roots in specific earlier experiences, EMDR provides a structured path through difficult material that produces meaningful change in a defined number of sessions rather than open-ended exploration.",
