  intro: "IFS therapy and EMDR in Piedmont, CA -- for anxiety, perfectionism, burnout, and the internal patterns that high-achievement environments generate and sustain long after the external pressures have changed. Piedmont is a small, academically competitive enclave in the East Bay where high standards are the baseline and visible struggle carries a particular social cost. The psychological patterns that develop inside that environment are specific: contingent self-worth tied to performance, an inner critic that monitors constantly and treats any faltering as a threat, anxiety that persists despite objectively good circumstances, and the particular exhaustion of never fully being able to let anything be good enough. IFS was designed to work with exactly these internal dynamics -- not by lowering standards but by changing the relationship with the parts that enforce them.",
