  intro: "IFS therapy and EMDR in San Leandro, CA -- for anxiety, trauma, depression, anger, and the internal patterns that have been building quietly for longer than they should have. San Leandro sits between Oakland and Hayward in the middle of the East Bay, a working city with a genuinely diverse population and fewer mental health providers per capita than the cities immediately north. Most residents looking for a therapist end up navigating Oakland or Bay Area options that require a commute that adds logistical friction to an already difficult decision. Telehealth removes that entirely. Quality IFS and EMDR therapy from home in San Leandro, without the drive and without settling for whoever happens to be geographically convenient.",
  localContent: "Marcus Ghiasi is a Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist offering telehealth therapy to San Leandro adults and East Bay residents. San Leandro's population is one of the most diverse in the East Bay -- economically, culturally, and occupationally -- and the approach here takes that diversity seriously. Cultural context shapes how distress is experienced and expressed, what help-seeking means within a family and community, and what approaches actually fit. Sessions are Wednesday through Friday from anywhere in California. IFS maps and works directly with the internal parts that drive anxiety, anger, avoidance, self-criticism, and the relationship patterns that feel automatic despite awareness of them. EMDR processes the experiences stored in the nervous system that continue to organize current reactions regardless of insight or time. A free 15-minute consultation is the starting point.",
