    "EMDR sessions process the specific experiences underlying anxiety, perfectionism, and life transition distress systematically. Each session targets a defined experience or memory network rather than exploring broadly, which means progress is trackable and the scope of the work is clear. For Pleasanton clients whose anxiety has roots in specific earlier experiences -- early academic pressure, performance failures, conditional acceptance -- EMDR targets those stored experiences directly and allows the nervous system to update rather than continuing to run historical programs.",
