    "Therapy starts with a free 15-minute consultation -- a direct conversation about what you are dealing with and whether working together makes sense. The first full session maps your specific situation and begins identifying the internal parts and patterns creating the most difficulty. Sessions are 45 or 60 minutes via secure telehealth video, available Wednesday through Friday from home or anywhere in California.",
    "IFS sessions involve getting to know the parts of your internal system with curiosity rather than judgment. The part that pushes, the part that criticizes, the part that is exhausted, the part that holds old pain. The work is not about eliminating these parts but understanding what they are protecting and building a more functional relationship with the whole system. EMDR sessions are more targeted, processing specific experiences that the nervous system has not fully resolved.",
