    "San Mateo's community has a stability and rootedness that distinguishes it from the more transient parts of the Peninsula -- and that stability creates its own specific psychological dynamic. Long-term residents navigating the question of whether the life they built here is still the one they want. Families whose children have left and who are reckoning with what comes next. Adults at midlife who have achieved significant goals and find themselves in unexpected emotional territory. These transitions do not always announce themselves as crises, but they are significant, and individual therapy is particularly well suited to working with them directly.",
