    "IFS sessions work with specific internal parts directly. For Marin City clients whose internal system developed in response to real adversity, this means working with parts that were built for environments that required significant protection -- and helping those parts understand that they do not have to work as hard in the current context. The work does not dismiss what those parts were responding to. It honors what they were for while helping the internal system update. That distinction matters and shapes every session.",
    "EMDR sessions process specific experiences or patterns of experience the nervous system has not fully integrated. For clients dealing with complex or accumulated trauma rather than a single event, the processing often involves working through layers of experience over multiple sessions rather than resolving a single incident. The bilateral stimulation activates natural processing capacity in a way that allows stored responses to update gradually and thoroughly. Most clients find the process more manageable than they expected because the work happens at the neurological level rather than requiring extensive verbal narration of difficult material.",
