    "CBT sessions in Oakland are structured and purposeful -- identifying specific thought patterns, examining the evidence for and against them, developing more accurate and functional alternatives, and building behavioral skills that reduce avoidance and increase engagement. For Oakland clients dealing with anger specifically, sessions focus on identifying the cognitive patterns maintaining anger at a problematic level and developing more accurate processing of the situations that trigger it. The work is direct and the progress is trackable rather than open-ended.",
    "Progress in CBT for Oakland clients typically moves in clear increments. Anxiety and depression work usually shows meaningful symptom reduction within 8 to 16 sessions. Anger work often shows change faster -- the cognitive patterns maintaining anger at a problematic level tend to respond quickly to direct examination. The skills developed in CBT continue working after formal therapy ends, which is one of the approach's significant advantages for Oakland residents whose lives do not pause for ongoing therapeutic work.",
