    "The consultation is 15 minutes -- a direct conversation about what is happening, how long it has been happening, and whether the approach here is the right fit. For Palo Alto men who have tried previous therapy and found it insightful but insufficient, the consultation focuses on whether IFS and EMDR address what previous work has not closed. No forms, no obligation. If working together makes sense, the first full session maps the internal parts most active in creating the difficulty and begins direct engagement with them. Sessions are 45 or 60 minutes via secure telehealth video, Wednesday through Friday.",
    "Men's therapy sessions in Palo Alto are structured and efficient -- sessions have clear focus and move toward concrete change rather than open-ended exploration. The work addresses what is actually creating problems -- the perfectionism, the anxiety, the relationship strain, the burnout -- and engages the internal parts driving those problems directly. For Palo Alto men who appreciate structured, outcome-oriented processes, IFS and EMDR fit that preference while producing change at a level that performance coaching and behavioral approaches do not reach.",
    "Progress in men's therapy in Palo Alto tends to move faster than clients expect given how long the patterns have been entrenched. The existing self-awareness and motivation that Palo Alto men typically bring accelerate the internal work. The inner critic does not disappear but its activity reduces when its underlying concerns are addressed directly. The driven part finds a different relationship with rest and recovery when its protective function is understood rather than overridden. Most men notice meaningful change within 12 to 20 sessions.",
